<!--
  切抜 — a column cut out of a page with scissors.

  Drawn to the five rules measured off the chanterelle in kinokocho/tools/make-art.py:
  one weight throughout, seven strokes to its eight, sitting four degrees off square,
  and nothing filled. Every edge is a run of nearly straight segments that change angle
  where the scissors bit again, at uneven intervals so the outline does not fall into a
  rhythm.

  The weight is no longer the chanterelle's 0.0143 of the drawing's width. The shop
  settled its launcher weights on 2026-09-17 against a measurement instead: mean ink at
  48px, the band 0.61 to 0.89. This mark came in at 0.24, the lightest of the nineteen.
  At strokeWidth 20 it measures 0.62, beside onsa and seizu at 0.64 and sokudokei at
  0.60. The number looks unlike theirs only because this drawing is on a 512 viewport
  where theirs are on 108: as a fraction of the canvas it is 3.1% against their 2.8%.

  ⚠ Measure this one WITH the group below applied. Desktop/icons/icontool.py renders
  paths only and drops the transform, and this is the one icon in the shop that has one,
  so ignoring the 0.84 makes it read about 16% heavier than the launcher draws it.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="512"
    android:viewportHeight="512">
  <!-- Scaled to 0.84. An adaptive icon only guarantees the central 72dp of 108,
       and a circular mask takes the corners of even that: the drawing's bounding
       circle is 78.6% of the canvas against a safe 66.7%, so at full size the
       launcher clipped the top, the bottom and both cut edges. -->
  <group
      android:pivotX="254.5"
      android:pivotY="257"
      android:rotation="-4"
      android:scaleX="0.84"
      android:scaleY="0.84">
    <path
        android:strokeColor="#000000"
        android:strokeWidth="20"
        android:strokeLineCap="round"
        android:strokeLineJoin="round"
        android:fillColor="#00000000"
        android:pathData="M132,104 L262,98 L374,108 L366,166 L376,232 L368,286 L378,366 L370,408 L244,416 L134,404 L141,330 L131,268 L139,186 Z" />
    <path
